# XDG - State directories
# `.claude/*` excludes top-level entries only — directory itself stays
# accessible, so the per-subdir negation rules below can re-include nested
# content. Per `man gitignore`: "It is not possible to re-include a file
# if a parent directory of that file is excluded."
.claude/*
# Shared team content (whitelisted — decisions, agents, workflows, skills).
# Directory entries MUST come before the `**` recursive entries so git's
# pattern matching re-includes the directory before evaluating the recursive
# pattern. Pattern matches mahavishnu's allowlist style. Per
# oneiric/docs/adr/0001-deployability-discipline.md.
!.claude/decisions/
!.claude/decisions/**
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents/**
!.claude/workflows/
!.claude/workflows/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
# PR-1c: SessionEnd hook + settings.json are part of the cross-repo
# merge-workflow infra (mahavishnu/.claude/hooks/agent-merge-on-end.py
# + .claude/settings.json). Track them so fresh clones ship the hook.
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**
!.claude/settings.json
.session-buddy/
.crackerjack/

# Git Worktrees
.worktrees/

# XDG - DELETE candidates
.obsidian/

.archives/
.backup/
.backups/

.coverage
.coverage*

